{"title":"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A set of positive integers is called <i>fragrant</i> if it contains at least two elements and each of its elements has a prime factor in common with at least one of the other elements.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/714f5b771a077d689c1b2fb3ba01ad7be51e21c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)=n^2+n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" />.  What is the least possible positive integer value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> such that there exists a non-negative integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for which the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/096f4d31ced33c7d415ee4bcf54720b421c2f206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{P(a+1),P(a+2),\\ldots,P(a+b)\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"272\" height=\"18\" /> is fragrant?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76a6ad5c6d55fd1d92a51ccad1dfd68daa994fb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />. We note that in order to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/26116950a97242a3036c86611f353b8ec9c9333a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/d/47d10de08f9e90833820c209351232fed3da4fdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid P(x+y)-P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" /> we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c948b2cfd26ccd285483fa9269528b17901af7ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid x^2+x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d7e1ac0597afae0f544be5696fee739eb449d8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid y(2x+y+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"132\" height=\"20\" />. It is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/5/805adb68e3d554fc089c7b8a55ce70ebe48115c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\equiv 1 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d6106b24a848e5445f5af2dc6de8bd5e81ea45a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid n^2+n+1 \\mid (2n+1)^2+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"21\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/7/8a7235032efcef3a66aa6278c43acd62ca4aec85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\tfrac{-3}{p} \\right)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3b4834614e5e7e189cb7d621cfb4fb0bd36dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d2d52291ec0fa4023257e7be5d864c2f87f954f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid 2x+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d731d82cd1be4647ea30839ae2b789f89abdb9e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" />. WLOG, we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6eea48f5ccd7d0b6183ba6ed0054674a5fa176eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=p-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" /> and see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c8443d38b78486f2b871b9d7b5b4e941bf813ac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\nmid x^2+x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"21\" />. So there doesn't exists <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21d89db737538bc041bd8edb0a78a91e917f2f79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd \\left( P(x),P(x+1) \\right)&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40ac4b6f5ab516ac6fe7132ed2fe7a1d77ca02dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b204c92eba3668d78a52e4aaaed6d1ab529c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid 2x+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> and we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/9/9c959f0f0d1762d4ce90e709d421cb8579321c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\tfrac{p-3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"64\" height=\"24\" />. Hence, from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c948b2cfd26ccd285483fa9269528b17901af7ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid x^2+x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"21\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f95fee4e5abb16c2f5c07c41672e3a97c63d2de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. So there is one prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f95fee4e5abb16c2f5c07c41672e3a97c63d2de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/260caea73846e2259cfb908e591cc9f6adbf59a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd \\left( P(x),P(x+2) \\right)&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b0e1404de4eca35c42876bcc83707b753e990e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, it is obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cfc82a82f113a7432ca68f71338c383bbcb44b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> satisfy and is the only answer.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45bc0006df273cb384b6c864236b3c1bf292e898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, we do the similar thing and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6f51b6f32f91b9cad596bb796ac73210bfc4f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid 2x+5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c948b2cfd26ccd285483fa9269528b17901af7ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid x^2+x+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"21\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65afa5337178022480485e22da271280652def87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />.\n___________________________\nNow, back to the problem, since there doesn't exists any prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3b4834614e5e7e189cb7d621cfb4fb0bd36dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/4/5e486f30ca8576f95b60e20db1cb1ac4afb651ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />. The only prime for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40ac4b6f5ab516ac6fe7132ed2fe7a1d77ca02dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f95fee4e5abb16c2f5c07c41672e3a97c63d2de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> so if we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08afd02574255fbd387b9717398620b6040f5966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\mid P(x+1), 7 \\mid P(x+3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"20\" /> then there will be a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/5/c05d4a1b9cb14a5c83a3365d669b36911951416f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\nmid P(x+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" /> remains. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/7/fa7c1f54c6cbf5d2785fa2b643167c004e2e7317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> since we need a prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/f/20f8ea199baaf8122e6e4304f8f00f7bb5231fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid P(x+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"96\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e60018eca0769b7fc651153bde576e16e360316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid P(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" /> but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1ddc12fbbcecee773a02a607c30356959ff649ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\ge 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/3462313daf303d8645046c6a56aebb7960d2469f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\ne 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f69c1ec597d19324140f3130e9d63367f4b69c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=5$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, we consider two cases, where there are two numbers that are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> (which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15c2e2350728ef2cfdc09735b2d46c6e8aafce23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 \\mid P(x+1), 19 \\mid P(x+5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"20\" />), the middle-three numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f496393c4ad5bff290c17bb0b90a91c3a1022f54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x+2),P(x+3),P(x+4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"228\" height=\"20\" /> we can't find a way make each two of them have common prime factor. If no two are divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> then they can only be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/dde5cee5c2e185ac93945c354c5c0deca40a7dc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" />, but it can't cover all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> \"consecutive\" numbers.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282cf257220cfc0de7647945572e6529c1d4774f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=6$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> then we can pick <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/6/d863a994bec5f8c773c98fe9c02da826bdd17da0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 \\mid P(x+2),P(x+6), 3 \\mid P(x+1), P(x+4), 7 \\mid P(x+3), 7 \\mid P(x+5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"569\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>So the final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/2/282cf257220cfc0de7647945572e6529c1d4774f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=6$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to the first solution; worded differently. \n</p><p>Define a prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> as a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e24b68c01c1ed9af845456bee60859be939ddc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\textit{-prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09e77893574a61113268482b27be3363936199ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n) \\equiv_p P(n+k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/e/13efbee84c5a448a4dcdd787c77c91a1cf82e9e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,k \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f4215ae3d48d6f2069bb1e8f74c349339ce51e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\equiv_p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> means mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />). We claim there are no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-primes, that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the unique <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-prime, that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the unique <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-prime, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is the unique <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-prime. First note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfd17dc4d3100462df726e8eb7f9262783429eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> is always odd so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is not a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />-prime for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81c18ad8c8fe7e8562660f28aeab0b4c29b70bce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{There are no } 1\\textbf{-primes}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"17\" />: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/4/9648ce3d2321d24f7cfc56fccf21af7d1347c26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n) \\equiv_p P(n+1) \\equiv_p 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/a/6ba18dee61d7431be5a7bade7bb136121e3756b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\equiv_p P(n+1)-P(n) \\equiv_p 2(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"272\" height=\"20\" />. And <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd2af6cc80b5e0545c157ec51829612bffc08be1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\neq 2 \\implies n+1\\equiv_p 0 \\implies P(n) \\equiv_p 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"307\" height=\"20\" />.  So no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-prime exists.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/f/d2f87be2bad75877965220292f3a93833da05222.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\textbf{ is the unique } 2\\textbf{-prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"17\" />: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/252581e1521990715053057fcbe4c68342ecb3af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n) \\equiv_p P(n+2) \\equiv_p 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37c7641b320612de624fcf64f56d5198e2441df8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\equiv_p P(n+2)-P(n) \\equiv_p 2(2n+3) \\implies 2n+3 \\equiv_p 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"423\" height=\"20\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfa826b6083f20e25449e48028aaf6ec352dd76d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\neq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8c023ae7e0d1c32b756fd67a156686c29eaab1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(n+2) \\equiv_p 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25be3bfc91860b9a2db10e36a3e4d6766abd5ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\equiv_p P(n+2) \\equiv_p 2^{-2} + 2^{-1} + 1 \\iff 0 \\equiv_p 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"356\" height=\"22\" />. Necessarily <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f95fee4e5abb16c2f5c07c41672e3a97c63d2de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />.  Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/adddd9a2a34768fa1b6dde4c9f8eeb238c69cb2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n+3 \\equiv_7 0 \\iff n \\equiv_7 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"17\" />, in which case one can check <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbe9e52217a42bd23d7a5ea5bd3183af186d1621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n+2) \\equiv_7 P(n+4) \\equiv_7 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is indeed a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-prime.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/5/e0588e0ce71262080764591ba2b5e5529b143eb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\textbf{ is the unique } 3\\textbf{-prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"17\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3b12109c7d661a1b72594ffd132af49131fd275.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n) \\equiv_p P(n+3) \\equiv_p 0 \\implies 0 \\equiv_p P(n+3) - P(n) \\equiv_p 6(n+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"504\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d609bca7d5520cd17c441cb5e026dc7e0f442c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\neq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cfc82a82f113a7432ca68f71338c383bbcb44b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/b/d1b4d27340f0c1e283ecb93571a5ca43575c5bea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+2 \\equiv_p 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"85\" height=\"19\" /> (the latter implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883a9be274dc67edcb04b8bf75e4a9dfa3a4ab34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n) \\equiv_p 3 \\equiv_p 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />). In either case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54cfc82a82f113a7432ca68f71338c383bbcb44b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. And <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44d4a25b2b46bcdf91a74fa71eab4c978e8e4902.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n) \\equiv_3 0 \\iff n \\equiv_3 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"187\" height=\"20\" />, which also implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/190f39385a4a3fd32d3d904bd0e813c0cac578f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n+3) \\equiv_3 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is indeed a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-prime. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/3/963883e0810d9da1290c93ad01a112e8edefa2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 \\textbf{ is the unique } 4\\textbf{-prime}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"205\" height=\"17\" />: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/3/4e355a2a4cff291a8d464c7d11531a27d9a627fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\equiv_p P(n+4) \\equiv_p P(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b068bf6cd41c6cd29555580244571c33d50a63c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\equiv_p P(n+4) - P(n) \\equiv_p 4(2n+5) \\implies 2n+5 \\equiv_p 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"423\" height=\"20\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/d/8ad0da416173fe1e39cd930caa18bfcf6c8450a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\neq 2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/7/a670c6509279863959d78cde68c402c86a2b20e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv_p -5/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" /> hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb63a97f4f24983ae5e401f810299580d5643b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\equiv_p P(n) \\equiv_p 25/4 - 5/2 + 1 \\implies 19 \\equiv_p 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" />. Necessarily <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65afa5337178022480485e22da271280652def87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />. And <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69b3786656268a0cb961d65dad6213bb9a890834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n+5 \\equiv_{19} 0 \\iff n \\equiv_{19} 7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"217\" height=\"17\" /> In which case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d17d480d254f6a57c305e5df1d76d811fac4451a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n) \\equiv_{19} 57 \\equiv_{19} 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/b/b8bf3d88a246cdbcd63ba7e4032e9ae11dc46d50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n+4) \\equiv_{19} 133 \\equiv_{19} 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" /> So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is indeed a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-prime. \n</p><p>This shows the claims. At this point its easy to see/show the smallest such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. On the other hand \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adff6001bf0907672157729d55fb07b6aab7f337.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  P(196) &amp;\\equiv_3 P(199) \\equiv_3 0 \\\\  P(197) &amp;\\equiv_{19} P(201) \\equiv_{19} 0 \\\\ P(198) &amp;\\equiv_7 P(200) \\equiv_7 0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"196\" height=\"68\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/3/093122b647035ac28825785a8b5f7f5a71af6f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{196,...,201\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" /> is fragrant. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO\" title=\"2016 IMO\">2016 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002115\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.050 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 638/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 22275/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.157      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.157      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17943:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018002115 and revision id 287241. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}